@component server-keys
@intent (re-distilled for Constellation v2.4.167 — key lifetime phases, §13.25.19; prior distillation verified vs reference @ v2.5.87, 2026-06-12) KEY-MGMT server-side sub-module of the Constellation live-board `server` family (v1.1 split per phase_2 2026-06-04). Owns the key registry for all four kinds (`upstream` uk-* · `collab` ck-* · `local` lk-* · `peer` pk-*) + issuance / list / revoke / label / renew / purge lifecycle + role classification authority + the shared admission predicate that decides an expired key's phase at both admission sites. Two stores: the legacy `ws-keys.json` registry (wire validity + role) and `key.json` keyStore (state, lifetime, provenance). **Expiry is not revocation**: expiry is a derived `phase` (active / standby / dormant), never a stored `REVOKED`; `revokedAt` is written only by an explicit revocation. **Carries C7 `@hazards` per phase_2 — credential surfaces with redaction discipline + filesystem integrity invariants.** Every management verb is an operator verb (§13.25.9); client gateway exposes commands via `gateway-client-key-mgmt.eux` but server has final say.
@expansion temperature=0.2 model=agent/claude template=estreux/v0.1
@targets vanilla
@profile backend-service
@source constellation/reference/runtime/server.cjs(KEY-MGMT block — keyStore / key* helpers + wsKeyIssue / wsKeyList / wsKeyRevoke / wsKeyLabel / wsKeyRenew / wsKeyPurge + keyExpiredRefusal admission predicate + keyExpirySweep) · Constellation.md §13.25.9–§13.25.19 · constellation/reference/WS-PROTOCOL-KEY-MGMT.md v0.5
@state
  KEY_JSON   : string = 'key.json'                  # keyStore persistence (5 stored states). 별도 legacy WS_KEYS='ws-keys.json' (role lookup) + local 키 파일 'local-keys/<label>.key'. 셋 다 gitignored MUST — credential files (v2.4.11 .gitignore 블록 key.json/ws-keys.json/local-keys/*.key 커버)
  keyStore   : {key, ref, label, kind, state, issuedAt, ttl, renewedAt?, renewCount, renewedBy?, lastAgent?, lastSeenAt?, revokedAt?, deletedAt?, expiredAt?, lastExpiryNoticePhase?, boundAgent?, roleDescription?, adoptedFromLegacy?}[]
  wsKeys     : {key, label, role, createdAt}[]      # legacy registry — an explicit revocation removes the entry; expiry does not
  KEY_TTL_CHOICES_DAYS : [15, 30, 90]               # closed set; ttl 0 only on legacy-adopted keys
  KEY_TTL_DEFAULT_DAYS : {local: 90, peer: 30, collab: 30, upstream: 30}
  KEY_GRACE_MS         : 3 days (env WS_KEY_GRACE_MS)   # standby window after max(expiresAt, lastSeenAt)
  access.keys.graceRenew : boolean = true           # operator policy — standby renewal on request
@deps
  fs       : key.json atomic write (tmp → fsync → rename, 0600) · ws-keys.json · local-keys/*.key
  crypto   : crypto.randomBytes → key issue (<prefix>-<24hex (randomBytes(12))>) · keyRef kr-<hex>
  -relay   : orchestration dispatch entry point (KEY_VERBS operator gate); AgentNameChanged after KeyLabel · ServerNotice key-expiry / key-renewed
  -core    : wsKeyRole(key) consumer (WS upgrade meta + /join/* gate) · shared admission predicate at upgrade (URL key) and HELLO (body key)
@ports
  cmd  wsKeyIssue(label, kind?, ttlDays? | ttl?, roleDescription?, boundAgent?) : ttl from the closed set (absent → kind default; outside / 0 → INVALID_TTL; unknown kind → UNKNOWN_KIND); persist → KeyIssued
  cmd  wsKeyList(includeRevoked?, includeDeleted?)    : rows with derived phase / graceUntil / ttlDays / ttlChoices; default omits revoked + deleted (standby / dormant are listed)
  cmd  wsKeyRevoke(keyRef | key, mode)                : explicit revocation — accepted in active / standby / dormant; ALREADY_REVOKED only in revoked / deleted; stamps revokedAt, removes the legacy entry
  cmd  wsKeyLabel(keyRef | key, newLabel)             : non-terminal states (expired keys included); AgentNameChanged to live holders
  cmd  wsKeyRenew(keyRef | key, ttlDays? | ttl?)      : new window from now, key string unchanged; clears expiredAt; repairs state REVOKED without revokedAt → ACTIVE / ISSUED; NOT_RENEWABLE on revoked / revoking / deleted; NO_EXPIRY on ttl 0
  cmd  wsKeyPurge(keyRefs?)                           : revoked (not REVOKED_PENDING) rows → tombstone (key null, deletedAt, state DELETED); row kept
  cmd  admissionPredicate(key, renewMarker)           : standby + marker + graceRenew → renew (renewedBy grace-request) + admit; otherwise ConnectionRejected{code key-expired, phase, renewable, graceUntil?, label, expiresAt, hint}
  cmd  wsKeyRole(key)                                 : lookup → 'upstream' | 'collab' | 'local' | 'peer' | null (unknown / explicitly revoked)
  out  KeyIssued(key | null for local, keyRef, label, kind, ttl, issuedAt, expiresAt, …)
  out  KeyListResult(keys[])
  out  KeyRevoked(key, mode, agentsDisconnected, agentsNotified)
  out  KeyLabeled(key, oldLabel, newLabel)
  out  KeyRenewed(keyRef, label, kind, ttl, issuedAt, renewedAt, expiresAt, wasLapsed, renewCount)
  out  KeyPurged(count, keyRefs, error?)
  out  ServerNotice{kind: key-expiry | key-renewed}    # notice group — wakes no agent
  out  ConnectionRejected{code: key-expired, phase, renewable}
  out  AgentNameChangedRequest                          # routed via -relay broadcast
@hazards
  # C7 — credential + filesystem integrity surfaces per eux-format v1.1 §2.5 @redaction (credential 한정) + §13.14 redaction discipline
  credential_surfaces:
    - keyStore[*].key / wsKeys[*].key                   # full key strings — MUST NOT log/expose unredacted to public traces, board fan-out, or committed transcripts
    - issuance_response_bodies                          # KeyIssued payload carries full key for non-local kinds
    - key_list_response_bodies                          # KeyListResult carries key strings for non-local kinds — operator-only verb; local rows carry null
    - revoked_rows_at_rest                              # revoked rows kept their key strings indefinitely until KeyPurge tombstones them (key → null)
    - filesystem_path: key.json + ws-keys.json + local-keys/*.key   # credential files — 전부 gitignored MUST, never commit
  redaction_discipline:
    log_surface: show only a fingerprint / prefix of a key; full key value NEVER logged
    human_surface: key-management replies are excluded from the meaningful-inbound set and masked on printing paths (§13.25.11 v2.4.159)
    operator_only: every key verb, KeyList included, is operator-gated (§13.25.9); no agent role other than main may enumerate
  integrity_invariants:
    key_json_atomic_write: temp file + fsync + rename (avoid torn write on crash; partial JSON breaks boot reload)
    key_json_load: parse failure → rename to key.json.corrupt-<ts>, start fresh (forensic evidence kept); rows with state REVOKED and no revokedAt normalized to ACTIVE / ISSUED with one log line (count)
    revoke_persistence_first: persist revokedAt to disk BEFORE force-closing connection (avoid revoke loss on crash mid-revoke)
    purge_save_visible: a failed save during KeyPurge is reported in the reply, never swallowed
  threat_model:
    public_log_leak: credential in stdout / committed transcript / public commit (mitigated by redaction_discipline)
    credential_file_commit: credential file accidentally committed (mitigated by .gitignore + pre-commit hook recommended)
    revoke_race: connection survives revoke if force-close persisted before revokedAt write (mitigated by revoke_persistence_first)
    expiry_as_revocation: expiry recorded as REVOKED makes a renewed key terminal on every management verb (mitigated by phase derivation — expiry never writes state or revokedAt)
    self_extension: a holder extending its own access (mitigated — only standby, only under the operator's graceRenew policy, only via the admission predicate; no agent-callable lifetime verb)
@routing
  authority_per_command:
    wsKeyIssue / wsKeyList / wsKeyRevoke / wsKeyLabel / wsKeyRenew / wsKeyPurge: operator verbs (KEY_VERBS) — main agent (host-local) or an authorized board connection; others get PERMISSION_DENIED
    admissionPredicate: server-internal at both admission sites; the renewal marker (URL renew=1 · HELLO renewRequest:true) is a request, the operator's graceRenew policy is the authority
    AgentNameChanged broadcast: server-initiated post-KeyLabel, no client authority required to receive
  trigger_message_names: [KeyIssue, KeyList, KeyRevoke, KeyLabel, KeyRenew, KeyPurge, RegisterUpstreamKey, RegisterCollabKey, RevokeUpstreamKey, RevokeCollabKey]    # -relay orchestration dispatch consumed
@redaction
  hook: pre-send + pre-log
  targets: [key strings (full), KeyIssued.key, KeyListResult rows' key, revoke reason fragments containing credential context]
  rationale: KEY-MGMT carries credential material that MUST NOT leak per §13.14 redaction discipline — public-repo redaction rules apply
@invariants
  # P3 AST 계약스키마 — phase_3 2nd cut per eux-format v1.2 §2.6 (EstreUX edd2fb7 — 4 sub-section state/temporal/transaction/causality + 17 vocabulary keyword).
  state:
    - kind 는 closed enum {upstream, collab, local, peer} member-of — unknown kind 는 UNKNOWN_KIND (absent → default upstream)
    - revokedAt 은 monotonic — once set, never null again; 명시 폐기(KeyRevoke / Revoke* alias) 만 set
    - expiry 는 state 에 쓰지 않음 — phase 는 read-time derived (active | standby | dormant | revoking | revoked | deleted)
    - ttl ∈ KEY_TTL_CHOICES_DAYS (ms) OR ttl == 0 (legacy-adopted only) OR a pre-v2.4.167 length awaiting its next renewal
    - key.json content 는 valid_json_pre OR valid_json_post 둘 중 하나 bounded (atomic write — torn-write 금지)
    - DELETED row 는 key == null (tombstone) — row 자체는 삭제하지 않음
  temporal:
    - phase standby holds while now < max(expiresAt, lastSeenAt) + KEY_GRACE_MS; dormant after
    - expiry sweep: before expiry at most once per key per day; after expiry once per phase change (lastExpiryNoticePhase), then silent
    - expiry sweep refreshes lastSeenAt of keys with an open connection (graceUntil follows use)
    - 동일 key 는 KeyRevoke after 동일 key string 재발급 없음 (no re-issue after revocation)
    - KeyRenew / standby renewal keep the key string unchanged
  transaction:
    - wsKeyRevoke: persist(revokedAt) precedes force-close(conn) — revoke_persistence_first
    - wsKeyIssue: validate kind + ttl → crypto.randomBytes → persist (key.json + ws-keys.json) → KeyIssued
    - standby renewal: renew + persist inside the admission predicate, before any board state is sent (refusal-before-payload ordering unchanged)
    - wsKeyPurge: tombstone eligible rows → save → KeyPurged{count, keyRefs} (save error surfaced in reply)
    - wsKeyLabel: update label persist-before AgentNameChangedRequest broadcast (commit-then broadcast)
  causality:
    - wsKeyRole(key) == null iff key unknown ∨ explicitly revoked (legacy entry removed); an expired key keeps its role and is decided by the admission predicate
    - ConnectionRejected{key-expired}.renewable == 'request' iff phase == standby (marker absent); == 'operator' iff phase == dormant
    - KeyRevoke immediate mode implies force-close (active conn 의 강제 종료)
    - operator authority check precedes every key verb's effect
@metamorphic
  # P4 property/metamorphic 후보 — phase_3 2nd cut per eux-format v1.2 §2.7 (EstreUX edd2fb7).
  round_trip:
    - wsKeyIssue → expire → wsKeyRenew: same key string admitted; state not REVOKED; phase active
    - wsKeyIssue → wsKeyRevoke → wsKeyPurge: row kept (deletedAt set, key null), wsKeyRole(key) == null
    - wsKeyLabel(key, A) → wsKeyLabel(key, B) → wsKeyLabel(key, A): label == A endstate (label round-trip)
  idempotency:
    - wsKeyPurge(already purged): count 0 (no further change)
    - wsKeyList 호출 결과 같은 시점 동일 (store 변경 없으면 idempotent)
    - renewal marker on an active key: no effect (never extends early)
  determinism:
    - phase(key, now) deterministic from stored fields + now
    - wsKeyRole 의 prefix-based 분류 deterministic (input key → output role 1:1)
@operation_discipline
  derive:
    credential_authority_split: server owns issuance + revoke + renew + purge; client gateway exposes commands but server enforces
    expiry_is_not_revocation: only an explicit revocation is terminal; standby renews on request under operator policy, dormant needs the operator's renew
    revoke_atomicity: persist-then-close ordering avoids revoke loss on mid-operation crash
